From: Gabriel Zim <235131889+zimcontent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:08:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(runner): the agent's tab is in front before a command

On one computer over a day, 17% of the agents' clicks and 41% of their
fills answered "The browser didn't answer within 33 s". Chrome starts
with the tabs it had (--restore-last-session) and agent-browser may hold
one that is in the background. A hidden page answers no pointer event, so
each mouse move of the press waited 5 s and the batch ended at its limit,
in headless Chrome and on the agents' desktops alike.

Before a command that needs the page, the runner asks the tab whether it
shows (document.visibilityState, at most once a second) and brings a
hidden one to the front with agent-browser's own tab switch. A live view
that opens does the same. It never fails a command, and a tab that stays
hidden is left for 30 s.

Measured on Chrome 156: a click, a list, a download link and a file
button went from 33 s (failed) to 0.7-0.9 s; a 30-character fill from
33 s (failed) to 3.3 s. ADR 0040 section 19.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
